  "question": {
    "text": "The disintegration energy $Q$ for the nuclear fission of ${ }^{235} \\mathrm{U} \\rightarrow{ }^{140} \\mathrm{Ce}+{ }^{94} \\mathrm{Zr}+n$ is ______ $\\mathrm{MeV}$.\nGiven atomic masses of ${ }^{235} \\mathrm{U}: 235.0439 u ;{ }^{140} \\mathrm{Ce}: 139.9054 u$,\n${ }^{94} \\mathrm{Zr}: 93.9063 u ; n: 1.0086 u \\text {, }$\nValue of $c^2=931 \\mathrm{MeV} / \\mathrm{u}$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "208",
  "solution": {
    "text": "${ }^{235} \\mathrm{U} \\rightarrow{ }^{140} \\mathrm{Ce}+{ }^{94} \\mathrm{Zr}+\\mathrm{n}$<br />Disintegration energy\n$\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{Q} & =\\left(\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{R}}-\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{p}}\\right) \\mathrm{c}^2 \\\\\n\\mathrm{~m}_{\\mathrm{R}} & =235.0439 \\mathrm{u} \\\\\n\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{p}} & =139.9054 \\mathrm{u}+93.9063 \\mathrm{u}+1.0086 \\mathrm{u} \\\\\n& =234.8203 \\mathrm{u} \\\\\n\\mathrm{Q} & =(235.0439 \\mathrm{u}-234.8203 \\mathrm{u}) \\mathrm{c}^2 \\\\\n& =0.2236 \\mathrm{c}^2 \\\\\n& =0.2236 \\times 931 \\\\\n\\mathrm{Q} & =208.1716\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
